==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Uncertain. See {{w|Hoosier|Wikipedia's article on the subject}} for theories.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈhuʒɚ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A native or resident of the U.S. state of [[Indiana]].
# Someone associated with {{w|Indiana University}}, for example as a student, alum, or sports team member, or as a fan. This is also the university's sports [[mascot]].
# {{lb|en|slang|St. Louis, Missouri}} An [[uneducated]], [[tasteless]] [[Caucasian]] person.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=Emily Giffin|title=The Emily Giffin Collection: Volume 2: Baby Proof|isbn=1466882999|passage="The mall? Belinda, mall pickups are for '''hoosiers'''," I say, St. Louis slang for white trash. "With femullets." [...] "But Jake's no '''hoosier'''."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=Pate McMichael|title=Klandestine: How a Klan Lawyer and a Checkbook Journalist ...|page=2|passage=Taken as a whole, the article portrayed Ray as an indigent, racist “'''Hoosier'''” (St. Louis slang for redneck) with an inept, habitual tendency to commit petty crimes.}}
# {{lb|en|US|historical}} A kind of [[cupboard]] or [[dresser]] with shelves, drawers, etc.; a [[kitchenet]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|resident of Indiana}} {{l|en|Indianan}}
* {{sense|tasteless Caucasian}} {{l|en|white trash}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Characteristic of or pertaining to the American state of [[Indiana]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1947|author=John Bartlow Martin|title=Indiana: An Interpretation|page=xi|passage=Less well known but perhaps even more interesting than Stephenson is Court Asher, the second "gentleman" from Indiana. Asher is a more convincing bigot than Stephenson, one more homegrown and more '''Hoosier''' than the puffed-up grand dragon, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Alden Studebaker|title=Hoosieritis: The Contagious Condition That Is Indiana|page=51|passage=That's not very '''Hoosier''', is it?}}
#* '''2009''', Alexander Lawrence, ''Blest Be the Tie'', book 1:
#*: “Somehow the tradition doesn't seem very '''Hoosier'''.”

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Indiana}} {{l|en|Indianan}}

